==Strategy==
Do not focus on variety: instead, bring as many [[Cat Combo]]s as you can and the few cats that will allow you to win. [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] is strongly recommended to slow the boss, as due to her extreme damage, any approach that relies on tanking Idi:Re or weakening her is doomed to fail. Being a {{4c}} stage, the same restrictions apply here. The support in the stage are all enemies that would normally be unthreatening but they are quite strong here. Make sure to have cats that can safely clear the peons because it would be devastating to lose after the boss is taken down.

Be ready, because this stage can either be a chaining battle with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or a long endurance battle. Either way, you have to have the mindset and technique to best this stage. It is heavily recommended to bring some kind of fast meat shield such as [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] or [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] to quickly waste [[Idi:Re]]'s attack. Units such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] or [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] may be used as secondary or specialist meatshields for the peons that can pose a significant threat due to helping [[Idi:Re]] push up to your base. If the player has attacking specialists for these threats, you may be able to use them to slowly chip down [[Idi:Re]] instead of using specialist meatshields. Another thing to note is [[Idi:Re]]'s full backswing cooldown, meaning her attack restarts immediately if she flinches. Combined with her Omni Strike doubling her range, it's necessary to bring fast meatshields that can intercept her before she nukes a group of units.

Remember to manage your money well. This stage gives very meager amounts of cash, and you will likely never have more than 3000 cash at one point. Keep an eye on your cash levels at all times when dealing with different peon waves, and only send out units when they are absolutely needed.

Good luck to those who are attempting this stage, you will most definitely need it.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]: The only dragon variant that's usable here, Li'l King Dragon can work incredibly well here to chip down Idi and deal with the peons.
*[[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] and Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]: Good midrangers who can effectively deal with all of the peons in the stage, and a fairly niche Curse which may be helpful in the case of Fried Chicken to remove Imperator Sael's Slow.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Since you're likely to only be able to bring one meatshield here, Ramen would be your best pick. Ramen has high health and is able to resist the Heavenly Hippoes. All in all, a very solid meatshield pick for this stage.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: As a very good generalist meatshield, Stone Cat can make a nearly invincible wall in front of Idi:Re to waste her attack animation. If you happen to use BioBone (the Research Combos [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] together), Stone Cat will have reduced recharge time and will stall Idi:Re with her peon support even more efficiently. Even without the Research Combo, Stone Cat can prove to be a very good meatshield and support versus Idi:Re.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] and [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: They're able to kill the Heavenly Hippoe very quickly, and in the case of Mushroom, also deal with Sael and Relic Doge effectively.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]]: With his Surge and anti-Relic Slow, he can almost completely shut down Idi as she is a lot less threatening without her high speed, restricting her ability to break through your front lines into your back lines. Other DPS units can be brought along to back Uril and prevent Idi from hitting him. While he is certainly more useful in his True Form, clearing Floor 50 in [[Infernal Tower]] is a far greater challenge in itself.
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]: Good Long-Distance DPS which can snipe peons hiding behind Idi, and her low cooldown makes her easily replacable.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Amazing waver that can help chip down the peon waves, with its high damage and reach. Don't expect for it to survive for too long, however, as due to its low health and high TBA, its not self sustainable and will not survive. It can work pre-TF.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]]: Good answer to beat down the Gory Darks with its Insane Damage vs Darks, but it MUST be level 43 to be able to consistently hit Gory Dark before being knocked back.
*Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]]: More effective than Assassin BearCat, but it needs its Attack and Massive Damage talents maxed out to be useful.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: If you know the timing, you can chain Bahamut against Idi to take massive parts of her health off at a time. This is extremely difficult to do, however, but even then, Bahamut can be used to erase massive parts of Idi's health. The Explosion Talent makes this even better, as the Explosion can also clear peons very effectively and third Explosion can deal extra damage to Idi as it lingers for long.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]]: If for some reason you have it already, Cone can actually survive a hit from pre-strengthened Idi at level 41, allowing for an amazing way to stall her while you chip her down with your other units, though if you were able to beat [[Kappy Kawano]] before this stage you would not struggle here.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: While they need to be timed to land a hit against anything here, Supercar can destroy the tanky Angelic Hippoes and Imperator Saels with ease. Beware that if they hit Idi, they will always cause her to attack again, though this can be used to your advantage.

